## Flags for compiler

## Using C++20
CXX_STD = CXX20

## Where to find headers, and the two XAD defines, in ONE assignment. Appending
## to a variable in a second line is a GNU make extension, and R CMD check warns
## on every Makefile in the tarball that uses one.
##
## XAD reaches its active tape through a __thread variable defined in odelia and
## read from here; because R dlopens odelia that resolves through a call on every
## active value's construction and destruction. Neither package contains a
## thread. XAD_USE_STRONG_INLINE is client-side by design and forces the AReal
## constructors inline, which they are not by default. Both must match odelia's
## Makevars exactly: a mismatch on the first is a storage-class conflict on a
## symbol whose mangled name does not change.
PKG_CPPFLAGS = -isystem../inst/include/ -DXAD_NO_THREADLOCAL -DXAD_USE_STRONG_INLINE

## ⚠️ NO -fno-stack-protector HERE, however tempting xad::DerivInfo's raw C
## arrays make it. R CMD check raises *Non-portable flags in variable
## 'PKG_CXXFLAGS'* on it, and it does not even do what it says: R places
## PKG_CXXFLAGS BEFORE the distro CXXFLAGS, so on Linux the later
## -fstack-protector-strong wins and this is inert. Where it does take effect is
## macOS/clang, which adds no hardening of its own -- so the one platform it
## reaches is the one platform it leaves unprotected.

